<!-- WHY VISIT -->
<section class="section"><div class="container">
  <div class="section-header reveal"><h2>Why Visit Zhangjiajie</h2><div class="divider"></div></div>
  <div class="why-grid">
    <div class="why-card reveal"><div class="why-icon">&#127956;</div><h3>Avatar Mountains</h3><p>Stand among the 3,000 quartz-sandstone pillars that rise impossibly from misty valleys — the real-life inspiration for the floating Hallelujah Mountains in James Cameron's Avatar.</p></div>
    <div class="why-card reveal"><div class="why-icon">&#127755;</div><h3>Heaven's Gate</h3><p>Scale the 999 steps to Tianmen Mountain's magnificent natural arch — a 131.5-meter hole through the mountain known as "Heaven's Gate." The winding 99-bend road below is one of the world's most dramatic drives.</p></div>
    <div class="why-card reveal"><div class="why-icon">&#127750;</div><h3>Record-Breaking Glass Bridge</h3><p>Cross the world's longest and highest glass-bottomed bridge, suspended 300 meters above Zhangjiajie Grand Canyon. At 430 meters long, walking on transparent glass above the abyss is both terrifying and exhilarating.</p></div>
    <div class="why-card reveal"><div class="why-icon">&#128167;</div><h3>Underground Wonderland</h3><p>Explore Yellow Dragon Cave, one of China's largest karst caves, filled with spectacular stalactites, stalagmites, underground rivers, and vast caverns lit with colorful lights — a subterranean world of natural artistry.</p></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<!-- TOP ATTRACTIONS -->
<section class="section section-alt"><div class="container">
  <div class="section-header reveal"><h2>Top Attractions</h2><div class="divider"></div></div>
  <div class="tours-grid">
    <div class="tour-card reveal">
      <div class="tour-image" style="position:relative;"><img loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/hero-silkroad.jpg" alt="Avatar Mountains" width="1200" height="800"><div class="tour-badge">#1</div></div>
      <div class="tour-body"><h3>Zhangjiajie National Forest Park</h3><p>China's first UNESCO Global Geopark and the heart of the Wulingyuan Scenic Area. Take the Bailong Elevator — the world's tallest outdoor lift — up to Yuanjiajie for views of the "Southern Sky Pillar" (now renamed Avatar Hallelujah Mountain). The Golden Whip Stream trail offers a gentler perspective from the valley floor.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="tour-card reveal">
      <div class="tour-image" style="position:relative;"><img loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/hero-silkroad.jpg" alt="Glass Bridge" width="1200" height="800"><div class="tour-badge">#2</div></div>
      <div class="tour-body"><h3>Zhangjiajie Grand Canyon Glass Bridge</h3><p>Set Guinness World Records for both height and length when it opened. The transparent glass panels look straight down 300 meters to the canyon floor. For thrill-seekers, there's also the world's highest bungee jump (260m) available on site. Book tickets well in advance during peak seasons.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="tour-card reveal">
      <div class="tour-image" style="position:relative;"><img loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/hero-silkroad.jpg" alt="Tianmen Mountain" width="1200" height="800"><div class="tour-badge">#3</div></div>
      <div class="tour-body"><h3>Tianmen Mountain (Heaven's Gate Mountain)</h3><p>Take the world's longest cable car (7.5 km) from downtown Zhangjiajie to the summit. Walk the thrilling cliff-hanging glass walkways including the "Walk of Faith" — a 60-meter glass skywalk. The 999-step staircase to Heaven's Gate is said to bring good fortune to those who climb it.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="tour-card reveal">
      <div class="tour-image" style="position:relat/assets/images/hero-silkroad.jpg" alt="Baofeng Lake"><div class="tour-badge">#4</div></div>
      <div class="tour-body"><h3>Baofeng Lake</h3><p>A serene, emerald lake nestled deep in the mountains, surrounded by sandstone peaks and dense forest. Take a traditional wooden boat ride while local Tujia singers serenade you from the shore. The reflection of peaks in the still water creates perfectly symmetrical photographs.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="tour-card reveal">
      <div class="tour-image" style="position:relative;"><img loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/hero-silkroad.jpg" alt="Yellow Dragon Cave" width="1200" height="800"><div class="tour-badge">#5</div></div>
      <div class="tour-body"><h3>Yellow Dragon Cave (Huanglong Dong)</h3><p>One of China's most impressive show caves with 15 km of explored passages. Highlights include the Dragon Palace — a cavern so large it could fit three football fields — and the "Magic Needle," a 19.2-meter stalagmite insured for 100 million yuan. Boat rides take you along the underground rivers.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<!-- BEST TIME TO VISIT -->
<section class="section"><div class="container">
  <div class="section-header reveal"><h2>Best Time to Visit</h2><div class="divider"></div></div>
  <div class="why-grid">
    <div class="why-card reveal"><div class="why-icon">&#127800;</div><h3>Spring (Apr-May)</h3><p>Beautiful weather (15-25&deg;C) with fresh green foliage and blooming azaleas. Misty mornings create the quintessential "floating mountains" effect photographers dream of. Rain is common but usually brief.</p></div>
    <div class="why-card reveal"><div class="why-icon">&#127774;</div><h3>Autumn (Sep-Nov)</h3><p>The most comfortable season — crisp, clear days (15-25&deg;C) and lower humidity. The autumn foliage turns the mountains gold and red. September-October is peak photography season with the best visibility for panoramic views.</p></div>
    <div class="why-card reveal"><div class="why-icon">&#9924;</div><h3>Summer (Jun-Aug)</h3><p>Warm (25-33&deg;C) and humid with frequent rain. The upside: waterfalls are at their most powerful and the mist creates dramatic atmosphere. Weekends and Chinese holidays bring crowds — arrive at park gates at opening time.</p></div>
    <div class="why-card reveal"><div class="why-icon">&#10052;</div><h3>Winter (Dec-Mar)</h3><p>Cold (0-8&deg;C) with occasional snow. Snow-covered pillars are a rare and spectacular sight. Significantly fewer visitors and lower prices. Tianmen Mountain's snow-dusted walkways and icicle-covered cliffs are breathtaking. Some glass walkways may close in icy conditions.</p></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<!-- SAMPLE TOURS -->
<section class="section section-alt"><div class="container">
  <div class="section-header reveal"><h2>Sample Tours Featuring Zhangjiajie</h2><div class="divider"></div></div>
